---@field VpcId? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.VpcId The ID of the VPC for the targets.
---@field HealthCheckProtocol? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.ProtocolEnum The protocol to use to connect with the target. The GENEVE, TLS, UDP, and TCP_UDP protocols are not supported for health checks.
---@field HealthCheckPort? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckPort The port to use to connect with the target.
---@field HealthCheckEnabled? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckEnabled Indicates whether health checks are enabled.
---@field HealthCheckIntervalSeconds? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckIntervalSeconds The approximate amount of time, in seconds, between health checks of an individual target.
---@field HealthCheckTimeoutSeconds? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckTimeoutSeconds The amount of time, in seconds, during which no response means a failed health check.
---@field HealthyThresholdCount? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckThresholdCount The number of consecutive health checks successes required before considering an unhealthy target healthy.
---@field UnhealthyThresholdCount? aws.elastic_load_balancing_v2.HealthCheckThresholdCount The number of consecutive health check failures required before considering the target unhealthy.
